From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AsteroidOS <pike@asteroidos>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 04:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] backports/bt: skip GET_MWS_TRANSPORT_CONFIG on MT6630

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [MT6630 controller-quirk workaround]

MT6630 advertises support for Get MWS Transport Layer Configuration in
Read Local Supported Commands, but returns an error (Unknown Connection
Identifier) when the 4.1 core issues it during hci_init4. That error aborts
HCI init, so hci0 never comes up (ENOTCONN). MWS coexistence is unused on
the watch, so skip the command.
---
--- a/backports/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
+++ b/backports/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
@@ -829,7 +829,7 @@
 		hci_req_add(req, HCI_OP_READ_LOCAL_CODECS, 0, NULL);
 
 	/* Get MWS transport configuration if the HCI command is supported */
-	if (hdev->commands[30] & 0x08)
+	if (0 && (hdev->commands[30] & 0x08)) /* MT6630 errors on GET_MWS_TRANSPORT_CONFIG, aborting init; skip */
 		hci_req_add(req, HCI_OP_GET_MWS_TRANSPORT_CONFIG, 0, NULL);
 
 	/* Check for Synchronization Train support */
